Hello there,

i want to solve the task to plot from R into a Java dialog of my application. So far i found some code snippets and comments in the internet. I adapted them to my needs - in particular i added a panel to a JDialog containing a button and the GDCanvas and i also changed the settings for ".setenv“. You may find the source code below.

When i run the program i encounter a strange behaviour which can be best explained by this video:
http://kabasumo.de/wordpress/blog/2015/10/23/plotting-from-r-into-a-java-jdialog/ <http://kabasumo.de/wordpress/blog/2015/10/23/plotting-from-r-into-a-java-jdialog/>

The following things happen:
- Before the dialog opens another windows opens with the title JAVAGD *active*
- Then the JDialog with the plot button opens
- After pushing the plot button tree times i see finally five windows on my screen: JAVAGD, JAVAGD(3), JAVAGD(4), JAVAGD(5), PlotDialog
- I can close all windows but one: the JAVAGD dialog

One guy on stack overflow has a similar code but claims that his code works (last posting on the page):
http://stackoverflow.com/questions/30210495/how-to-visualize-my-r-plot-in-my-jframe-with-javagd <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/30210495/how-to-visualize-my-r-plot-in-my-jframe-with-javagd>

Whats my mistake? 

Thank you in advance
Bastian


